## Hardware design choices

*Main components:*
- STM32F411RCT6 microcontroller
- Ada-fruit 6050 USB type-C breakout board
- AP2112K-3.3TRG1 Voltage regulator 
- Waveshare 2inch LCD Display Module
- TDK PS1240P02BT Buzzer

*Microcontroller*
The selected microcontroller is the STM32F411RCT6, which belongs to the entry-level STM32F4 series of microcontrollers and offers good performance and versitile basic functionalities in a cost-effective package.

Microcontrollers in the STM32F4 series feature a wide range of pheripherals, such as serial communication interfaces and timer functions, which simplify embedded system implementation and reduce the need for external components.
The high clock frequency of the microcontroller enables fast operation in real-time applications. In addition, it's digital signal processing capabilities and floating-poin unit (FPU) improve performance in computionally
intensitive tasks. The selected microcontroller meets the technical requirements of the system and enables the planned dunctionalities to be implemented reliably.

The microcontroller's datasheet was carefully reviewed to identify all critical requirements related to it's electrical connections. All connections were implemented in accordance with the manufacturer's spesifications and 
recommendations to ensure reliable operation. 

28 I/O pins were left unused after adding all planned components and they were used for GPIO-pins. 

